#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn how to install snap from the Arch User Repository, enable its socket, "
"enable AppArmor, enable classic support, and test with hello-world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:8
msgid "Install snap on Arch Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:10
msgid ""
"On Arch Linux, *snap* can be installed from the [Arch User Repository (AUR)]"
"(https://aur.archlinux.org/packages/snapd/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:12
msgid ""
"The [manual build process](https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/"
"Arch_User_Repository#Installing_and_upgrading_packages) is the Arch-"
"supported install method for AUR packages, and you'll need the "
"[prerequisites](https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/"
"Arch_User_Repository#Getting_started) installed before you can install any "
"AUR package. You can then install snap with the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:14
msgid ""
"git clone https://aur.archlinux.org/snapd.git\n"
"cd snapd\n"
"makepkg -si\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:20
msgid ""
"Once installed, the *systemd* unit that manages the main snap communication "
"socket needs to be enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:22
msgid "sudo systemctl enable --now snapd.socket\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:26
msgid "Confinement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:28
msgid ""
"To take advantage of {ref}`Snap confinement <explanation-security-snap-"
"confinement>` and application sandboxing, ensure AppArmor is installed and "
"enabled by [following this guide](https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/"
"AppArmor#Installation), then run the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:30
msgid "sudo systemctl enable --now snapd.apparmor.service\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:34
msgid ""
"To test whether confinement is running correctly, install the [hello-world]"
"(https://snapcraft.io/hello-world) snap and run `hello-world.evil`. If "
"confinement is working, you will see a permission denied error:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:36
msgid ""
"$ hello-world.evil \n"
"Hello Evil World!\n"
"This example demonstrates the app confinement\n"
"You should see a permission denied error next\n"
"/snap/hello-world/29/bin/evil: 9: /snap/hello-world/29/bin/evil: cannot "
"create /var/tmp/myevil.txt: Permission denied\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:44
msgid "Classic support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:46
msgid ""
"To enable *classic* snap support, enter the following to create a symbolic "
"link between `/var/lib/snapd/snap` and `/snap`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:48
msgid "sudo ln -s /var/lib/snapd/snap /snap\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:52
msgid ""
"Either log out and back in again, or restart your system, to ensure snap’s "
"paths are updated correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:54
msgid ""
"To test your system, install the [hello-world](https://snapcraft.io/hello-"
"world) snap and make sure it runs correctly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/arch-linux.md:56
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap install hello-world\n"
"hello-world 6.3 from Canonical✓ installed\n"
"$ hello-world\n"
"Hello World!\n"
msgstr ""
